SUMMARY:Science Detectives: Pollinator Power
DESCRIPTION:Join us for classes designed especially for homeschool and track-out students. These 60-minute classes allow us to delve deeper into topics and incorporate additional learning experiences. \nDiscover the pollination power of bees\, butterflies\, bats\, and more! We’ll learn how pollination works through pollinator games and crafts\, and meet some unique animal pollinators\, too. \nParticipants must be 5-7 years old for this program. \nThis is a drop-off program\, but adults must stay in the Museum during the program time. \nREGISTER NOW!\nRegistration ends 48 hours prior to program start time. \nFor more information contact Missy Chernick.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/science-detectives-pollinator-power/
LOCATION:Downtown Raleigh\, 11 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Children,Classes,Homeschool/Track-Out Classes,K-12 Students,Science Detectives
